Sun Sep 13 06:20:22 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to version 2.8.2 (major jump from 0.7.1, bzlmod-only):
  * WORKSPACE support was removed in 2.0.0, consume via MODULE.bazel
  * Compatible with Bazel 7.4.x+, 8.x, 9.x LTS and rolling releases
  * Xcode rules forked from Bazel built-in Starlark into apple_support
  * Rules-based Apple toolchain with feature injection and sanitizer,
    layering_check, code coverage and param-file support
  * Dropped Bazel 6 support, armv7k watchOS and the -objc_abi_version
    linker flag; minimum tools version is macOS 11.0
  * Run obs_scm service in manual mode, it was left disabled
  * Refresh rpmlintrc for the renamed filelist check and the
    upstream data scripts shipped under /usr/src

